an, E. Ghorbani, H. R. Maimani, F. Rahimi Mahid\nDate: Mon Aug 12 07:38:44 2019\n\nThis paper deals with some of the algebraic properties of Sierpi\\'nski graphs and a family of regular generalized Sierpi\\'nski graphs. For the family of regular generalized Sierpi\\'nski graphs, we obtain their spectrum and characterize those graphs that are Cayley graphs. As a by-product, a new family of non-Cayley vertex-transitive graphs, and consequently, a new set of non-Cayley numbers are introduced. We also obtain the Laplacian spectrum of Sierpi\\'nski graphs in some particular cases, and make a conjecture on the general case.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJ. Kovič et al.: The Sierpiński product of graphs 21 (https://scispace.com/pdf/the-sierpinski-product-of-graphs-1r0hy4x9.pdf)\nciteturn0search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.2 years ago; Kovič et al.: The Sierpiński product of graphs 21 ... Then the group* Â(G, G, f) *is a semidirect product,* ... By Proposition 3.23, every element of Â(G, G, f) can be written as a product of a diagonal automorphism and an element from B̂(G, G, f).\nJ. Kovič et al.: The Sierpiński product of graphs 21\n\n**Proposition 3.24.** *Let G be a connected graph and let f : V(G) → V(G) be an automorphism. Then the group* B̂(G, G, f) *is a normal subgroup of the group* Â(G, G, f).\n\n*Proof.* Observe that the function λ : Â(G, G, f) → Â(G, f) defined by λ : Ψ(α, β) → Ψ(α, f ◦ α ◦ f⁻¹) is a homomorphism of groups, with B̂(G, G, f) being its kernel. Therefore, B̂(G, G, f) is a normal subgroup of Â(G, G, f).\n\n**Theorem 3.25.** *Let G be a connected graph and let f : V(G) → V(G) be an automorphism. Then the group* Â(G, G, f) *is a semidirect product,*\n\nÂ(G, G, f) = Â(G, f) × B̂(G, G, f).\n\n*Proof.* The group B̂(G, G, f) is a normal subgroup of Â(G, G, f) by Proposition 3.24. By Proposition 3.23, every element of Â(G, G, f) can be written as a product of a diagonal automorphism and an element from B̂(G, G, f). Moreover, only the identity is in both Â(G, f) and B̂(G, G, f). This proves that Â(G, G, f) is a semidirect product of Â(G, f) and B̂(G, G, f).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndLib.si - Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs (https://www.dlib.si/details/URN%3ANBN%3ASI%3Adoc-05TQJS6H)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.0 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; # Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs\n\n# Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs\n\nImage: tab1\n\n1. PDF datoteka (431 kB)\n\n1. TXT datoteka (43 kB)\n\n   Izvoz v EndNote (RIS format)\n\nAvtor(ji)\n\nFarrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan,, Mohammad (avtor)\nGhorbani, Ebrahim (avtor)\nMaimani, Hamid Reza (avtor)\nMahid, Farhad Rahimi (avtor)\n\nJezik\n\nangleški\n\nVir\n\nArs mathematica contemporanea\n\nLeto\n\n2021\n\nŠtevilčenje\n\nletnik 20, številka 2\n\nVsebina\n\nCayleyjev graf   graf Sierpińskega   Laplaceov operator   ne-Cayleyjevo število   spekter\n\nZaložnik\n\nUniverza na Primorskem, Fakulteta za matematiko, naravoslovje in informacijske tehnologije\n\nIzvor\n\nUniverza na Primorskem, Fakulteta za naravoslovje, matematiko in informacijske tehnologije\n(Obvezni izvod spletne publikacije)\n\nOpis\n\nV članku obravnavamo nekaj algebrajskih lastnosti grafov Sierpińskega in družino regularnih posplošenih grafov Sierpińskega. Za družino regularnih posplošenih grafov Sierpińskega določimo njihov spekter in karakteriziramo tiste grafe, ki so Cayleyjevi grafi. Poleg tega vpeljemo novo družino ne-Cayleyjevih vozliščno tranzitivnih grafov in, temu ustrezno, novo množico ne-Cayleyjevih števil. Določimo tudi Laplaceov spekter grafov Sierpińskega v nekaj posebnih primerih, postavimo pa tudi hipotezo v zvezi s splošnim primerom.\n\n\nURN\n\nURN:NBN:SI:doc-05TQJS6H\n\nCOBISSID\n\n91633411\n\nDOI\n\n10.26493/1855-3974.2199.97e\n\nObjavljeno\n\n22.11.2022\n\nMetapodatki\n\nCitiranje\n\nAPA:\n\nFarrokhi Dera